			"Message": "refactor(Output): Rename GPU directory casing and add WebKit DCL polling patch\n\nStandardize the `Terminal/Gpu` directory path to `Terminal/GPU` across both `Source` and `Configuration` trees to align with the project's PascalCase naming convention.\n\nAdditionally, extend the `Webview/Iframe/Service/Worker` transform to address a critical WebKit rendering deadlock. In Tauri's WKWebView context, the `DOMContentLoaded` event fails to fire on dynamically created inner iframes (WebKit bug #33604), causing the editor webview to hang on the `fake.html` placeholder. The existing VS Code fallback logic (`!options.allowScripts && isSafari`) is insufficient for Tauri. This patch removes the `allowScripts` guard, enforcing a polling-based fallback for all Safari/WebKit runtimes regardless of the sandbox configuration. A soft-fail mechanism for `crypto.subtle` checks is also added to prevent crashes in custom protocol contexts.\n\nThe build output artifacts in `Configuration` are regenerated to reflect these source transformations.",
			"SHA": "013a022ba7e66c25346b994382d6de5557b5bc3f"
		},
